<title>USA: Near-normal temps expected for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>Near-normal temps expected for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A storm system expected to form along the coast of Uruguay over the weekend should not bring cold air into Brazil's coffee belt, Weather Services Corp said in an update issued Thursday.</p>
<p>According to WSC, no cold air is forecast to build in behind the system. &quot;It appears that the cold air is trapped over southeast Argentina with no ability to come north,&quot; WSC stated.</p>
<p>Clouds increased across the region this morning. Showers and thunderstorms are expected to develop. Low temperatures this morning are in the 50s F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>The outlook calls for mostly cloudy skies during the next 5-7 days with episodes of scattered showers and thunderstorms. Temperatures should remain near normal levels with lows in the 50s to low 60s F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>There is no damaging cold expected, according to WSC.</p>
<p>	    ((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
